STARTER Configurable Adapter
============================

1. OVERVIEW
===========

starter-configurable-adapter (STCA) loads one plugin to talk to an
external source and exposes a numeric snapshot over a peer D-Bus TCP
API (org.starter.Adapter). An optional HTTP/JSON API can be enabled for
debugging. STCS connects with adapter-transport. This tree ships the
core and the in-tree `dummy` example; product plugins are separate repos.

Read path:

  plugin → data-ready → adapter store → D-Bus DataChanged / GetData
  → STCS adapter-transport + json-reader → starter STInput

Write path:

  starter STOutput → STCS json-writer + adapter-transport → SetData
  → stca_plugin_write_value(s) → external source

For the technical manual:

    $ make -C doc info   # Info
    $ make doc           # PDF (needs TeX)

2. PREREQUISITES
================

* GLib 2.0 / GObject / GIO / GModule (libglib2.0-dev)
* libxml2 (libxml2-dev)
* json-glib (libjson-glib-dev)
* libsoup 3.x or 2.4 >= 2.58 (libsoup-3.0-dev or libsoup2.4-dev)
* Autotools (autoconf, automake, libtool)
* Texinfo (makeinfo) to build the manual; TeX for PDF

3. BUILDING FROM SOURCE
=======================

    $ ./autogen.sh
    $ ./configure
    $ make
    $ sudo make install

4. RUNNING
==========

    $ starter-configurable-adapter --config /path/to/adapter.stca.xml

See examples/dummy/ for a temporary plugin that exercises the D-Bus API.
Out-of-tree plugins are built separately and loaded with `--plugin-dir`.
Optional HTTP: `--enable-http --http-port=N` or XML enable-http /
http-listen-port. Details are in the Texinfo manual.

